course: dictionary
lesson: 491
title: Ashore: onto the land
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ashore is a word about direction. It means on or onto the land after coming from the sea or a river. You can find it in stories about sailors and in lessons about the beach. «The crew rowed ashore singing» tells you the sailors left the boat and went onto the land.
explain: Look for the clue words around ashore. Sea, boat, river, and waves all point to water, so ashore must be the land next to it. Think of ashore as the opposite of being out at sea.
explain: Ashore often comes with other words: go ashore, come ashore, wash ashore, and run ashore. A ship can run ashore, which means it hits the land by accident. Something that washes ashore has been carried by the waves onto the beach.
fact: Ashore means on or onto the land, from the sea or a river.
fact: «When a hurricane comes ashore, its winds push the sea up into a wall of water.» Here ashore shows the storm moving from the sea onto the land.
fact: «The crew rowed ashore singing» means the sailors rowed their boat from the sea onto the land.
fact: Ambergris is a waxy lump that can «wash ashore», so it can be carried by the waves onto a beach.
fact: Swimmers should come ashore if the flag shows danger, so they leave the water and stand on the land.
exercise: «The crew rowed ashore singing, pulling the long bobbing procession of casks.» Where did the crew go? | Up into the sky | *Onto the land from the sea | Down into the deepest part of the sea | Around the ship in circles
exercise: Ambergris can «wash ashore». What does wash ashore mean? | Sink to the bottom of the sea | Float away into the sky | Be cleaned in the sea | *Be carried by the waves onto the land
exercise: A lifeguard blows a whistle and tells swimmers to come ashore because the flag shows danger. Why must they come ashore? | *So they get out of the water and onto the land | So they can go and buy an ice cream | Because the sea is warm and they want to sunbathe | Because the sea has turned into sand
test: When a hurricane comes ashore, what is it moving onto? | Round the back of a mountain | *Onto the land from the sea | Under the sea | Up into the clouds
test: Which word or phrase is the opposite of ashore? | *Out at sea | Upstairs | Under a bridge | Round the corner
exam: «Ambergris can wash ashore after a storm.» Where does the ambergris end up? | Floating high in the sky | *On the beach, on the land from the sea | Inside a perfume factory | Stuck at the bottom of the sea
